LOCATION:MERRILL HALL (MUSIC) / MUSIC\, JACOBS SCHOOL OF
GEO:39.164792;-86.518299
SUMMARY:A Well-Advised Lunch with CMS Past President Brian Kai Chin
DESCRIPTION:Students\, sign up here &gt\;  Meet one of the country's lead
 ing cultural entrepreneurs\, founding director of Common Tone Arts and mo
 st recently\, director of the Moores School of Music at the University of
  Houston!Brian Kai Chin (https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?
 url=https%3A%2F%2Fbriankaichin.com%2F&amp\;data=05%7C02%7Crumthun%40iu.ed
 u%7Cd16e448ec7ca466f197d08df418c4bc1%7C1113be34aed14d00ab4bcdd02510be91%7
 C1%7C0%7C639301742947185975%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRyd
 WUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7
 C0%7C%7C%7C&amp\;sdata=udOGD0U66hQIlkj%2BCdTNhQ5B0EiCy3Bs2r7KFI7Btas%3D&a
 mp\;reserved=0)is immediate past president of the College Music Society. 
 During his year with the org\, he led an innovation think tank to reimagi
 ne music schools. This is a great opportunity to discuss the future of ou
 r profession – for both students and faculty in the Jacobs School of Mu
 sic.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span data-ogsc="rgb(153\, 0\, 0)"><a id=
 "OWA7730098c-0734-52e1-4c3b-583deb07387f" class="x_OWAAutoLink" title="Or
 iginal URL: https://app.joinhandshake.com/events/2063258/share_preview. C
